From 1affa268375530b0e8fd10da87974ba5bddab0d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Rivers <mark.rivers@siemens.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:04:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] screen: Do not require both keyboard and mouse

mks_screen_setup() only accepted a console when the same object also
provided a keyboard and a mouse. Which of these interfaces QEMU exports
depends on its Display1 capabilities, and a console without them was
dropped, so no screen was shown at all.

A console is all that is needed to show a screen. Return success when
it is present. Keyboard, mouse and touch input stay optional, and
MksDisplayPicture already ignores input events while one of them is
missing.

Based on commit 5afe45f of the ANA libmks fork.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Haseeb Ashraf <haseeb.ashraf@siemens.com>
---
 lib/mks-screen.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/mks-screen.c b/lib/mks-screen.c
index bc8db2b..a01bf70 100644
--- a/lib/mks-screen.c
+++ b/lib/mks-screen.c
@@ -210,9 +210,10 @@ mks_screen_setup (MksDevice     *device,
         self->touchable = _mks_device_new (MKS_TYPE_TOUCHABLE, device->session, object);
     }
 
-  return self->console != NULL &&
-         self->keyboard != NULL &&
-         self->mouse != NULL;
+  /* Keyboard/mouse may be absent depending on exported Display1 capabilities.
+   * A console is sufficient to expose a usable screen.
+   */
+  return self->console != NULL;
 }
 
 static void
